{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes"],"declarations":40,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEight_eigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEight_eigenphase","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L393-L410","doc":"**Full eigenphase certificate (PROVED, compile-pending).**  For the\nfigure-eight operator `M = M_{4₁}` on `V_(2,1)` with `|tr M| ≤ 2`,\nthere is a real q-Reeb phase `θ` whose unit-circle pair `e^{±iθ}` is\nthe eigenvalue pair of `M`: product = `det M = 1`, sum = `tr M`.\nThis is the rigorous form of the manuscript proof sketch\n(figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md:1-36): det = 1, real trace ⇒\neigenvalues `e^{±iθ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenvalue_sum_eq_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenvalue_sum_eq_trace","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L361-L391","doc":"**Eigenvalue sum = trace (PROVED, compile-pending).**  Once\n`2 cos θ = tr M`, the complex pair `e^{±iθ}` has sum\n`e^{iθ} + e^{−iθ} = 2 cos θ = tr M`.  Proved over `ℂ` from\n`Complex.exp_mul_I` (Euler) and `Complex.cos`/`Complex.sin`\nparity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenvalue_prod_eq_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenvalue_prod_eq_det","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L350-L359","doc":"**Eigenvalue product = det (PROVED, compile-pending).**  Once\n`2 cos θ = tr M` and `det M = 1`, the complex pair `e^{±iθ}` has\nproduct `e^{iθ}·e^{−iθ} = 1 = det M`.  Proved over `ℂ` via\n`Complex.exp_add`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenphase_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.eigenphase_exists","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L335-L348","doc":"**Eigenphase existence (PROVED, compile-pending).**  For a real\nSL₂ matrix `M` (`det M = 1`) with `|tr M| ≤ 2`, there exists a real\nangle `θ` such that `2 cos θ = tr M`.  This `θ` is the q-Reeb\nrotation phase; the eigenvalues are `e^{±iθ}`.  Proved via\n`Real.cos_arccos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEightOp_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEightOp_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L311-L321","doc":"**det M_{4₁} = 1 (PROVED, compile-pending).**  The figure-eight knot\noperator on `V_(2,1)` has determinant 1: `det((σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²) =\n(det σ₁)² (det σ₂⁻¹)² = (−1)²(−1)² = 1`.  This is the\nmanuscript's det = 1 claim (figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md:33-34),\nhere proved by `det_mul` + the concrete generator determinants —\nNOT the `(−1)^4 = 1` numerology of the existing stub. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEightOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.figureEightOp","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L304-L309","doc":"**Figure-eight operator `M_{4₁} = (σ₁ σ₂⁻¹)²` on `V_(2,1)`.**\nBuilt from two Hoefsmit generator blocks `σ₁` and (the inverse of)\n`σ₂`.  We form `σ₁ · σ₂⁻¹` then square it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.invMatrix_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.invMatrix_det","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L295-L300","doc":"The inverse block has determinant `−1` (same as `σ`, since the knot\noperator det is `(det σ)²·(det σ⁻¹)² = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.invMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.invMatrix","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L288-L293","doc":"**The inverse generator block `σ⁻¹` also has determinant `−1`.**\n`σ⁻¹ = σ − h·I` has eigenvalues `q⁻¹, −q` (manuscript:17-19), so its\ndeterminant is `q⁻¹·(−q) = −1`.  Concretely `σ⁻¹ = (1/det)·adj(σ) =\n−adj(σ)` for `det = −1`, i.e. `[ −d, b; c, −a ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix_trace","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L283-L286","doc":"**The generator block has trace `h = q − q⁻¹`** (eigenvalue sum\n`q + (−q⁻¹) = q − q⁻¹`).  Concrete, by `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix_det","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L276-L281","doc":"**The generator block has determinant `−1`** (eigenvalues `q`,\n`−q⁻¹`).  Concrete from the Hecke constraint, not asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.matrix","kind":"def","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L272-L274","doc":"The 2×2 matrix of the generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.det_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.det_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L268-L268","doc":"Hecke determinant constraint: `det σ = a_ρ(h−a_ρ) − b² = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.h","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L266-L266","doc":"Hecke trace `h = q − q⁻¹` (so the other diagonal is `h − a_ρ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.b","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L264-L264","doc":"Off-diagonal entry `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.aρ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.aρ","kind":"def","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L262-L262","doc":"Diagonal entry `a_ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen.mk","kind":"ctor","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L260-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.HoefsmitGen","kind":"structure","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L249-L268","doc":"**Hoefsmit generator block on `V_(2,1)`.**  The concrete real 2×2\nmatrix of a Hecke generator `σ_i` in the Hoefsmit seminormal form,\nparameterised by the diagonal entry `a_ρ` and the off-diagonal `b`,\nwith second diagonal entry fixed by the Hecke trace `tr σ = h`\n(so `a_{−ρ} = h − a_ρ`) and `det σ = −1`.\n\nWe carry `(a_ρ, b, h)` and require the determinant constraint\n`a_ρ (h − a_ρ) − b² = −1`, which is the Hoefsmit relation\n`b = √(1 − a_ρ²)` rewritten with the Hecke trace `h`.  This is the\nmanuscript's `a_ρ a_{−ρ} − b² = det σ = −1`\n(figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md:30-31). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.det_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.det_mul","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L242-L245","doc":"**Determinant is multiplicative** — `det (M N) = det M · det N`.\nThe Cauchy–Binet / Binet identity at 2×2, proved by `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.mul","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L235-L240","doc":"2×2 matrix multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.det","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L232-L233","doc":"Determinant of a 2×2 matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.trace","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L229-L230","doc":"Trace of a 2×2 matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.d","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L225-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.c","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L224-L224","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.b","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.a","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L222-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.Mat2","kind":"structure","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L219-L225","doc":"A real 2×2 matrix is recorded by its four entries.  We only need its\ntrace and determinant for the eigenphase computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp_append","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L188-L195","doc":"**Derived: the surface-ordered exponential is multiplicative under\nbraid concatenation** (conditional on the §3b-cond class). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp_append_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp_append_letter","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L177-L186","doc":"**Derived (conditional on the §3b-cond class): the surface-ordered\nexponential carries the Markov cocycle.**  Given the Yekutieli\nreduction, the surface integral of an extended braid word is the\nsurface integral times the new letter — fully derived from\n`heckeImage_append_letter`, with the Stokes theorem as the only\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.stokes_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.stokes_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L175-L175","doc":"**Yekutieli non-abelian Stokes (axiomatised hypothesis).**  The\nsurface-ordered exponential equals the boundary ordered product\n(the Hecke image `ρ(β)`).  This is the deep theorem — see\nYekutieli (2015) §3; NOT provable from the finite-product machinery\nalone, so it is a class field, not a Lean proof.\nRef: [yekutieli2015] https://doi.org/10.1142/9537 §3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.surfaceOrderedExp","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L168-L168","doc":"The surface-ordered exponential of the categorical connection over\nthe Young-diagram braid surface of the braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.YekutieliSurfaceToBoundary","kind":"class","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L155-L175","doc":"**§3b-cond class: the Yekutieli surface→boundary reduction.**  The\nsingle axiomatised hypothesis: the surface-ordered exponential of the\ncategorical connection `α` over the braid surface equals the boundary\nholonomy, which (Part 1) is the Hecke image `ρ(β)`.  An instance of\nthis class is the only `sorry`-equivalent input; everything\ndownstream is then derived.\n\n`surfaceOrderedExp` is the abstract surface-ordered exponential\n`MI₂(d_α β; σ)`; the field asserts it equals the boundary holonomy of\nthe braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.toyModel_is_constant_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.toyModel_is_constant_word","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L136-L143","doc":"**The toy `z^ℓ` model is the degenerate single-generator case.**\nThe pre-#1627 scalar model `braidSurfaceMultTrace z n = z ^ n` is the\nHecke image of the constant word `[z, …, z]`; the genuine ordered\nproduct strictly generalises it (distinct letters give distinct,\nnon-commuting factors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_cyclic_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_cyclic_one","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L124-L134","doc":"**Closure invariance up to conjugation (class function).**  The\nMarkov-trace closure `tr_M ∘ ρ` is a class function, so the boundary\nholonomy is well-defined on cyclic words up to conjugation.  We prove\nthe one-letter cyclic rotation: rotating the head letter to the tail\nconjugates the Hecke image.  (Markov trace, being a trace, is then\ninvariant: `tr(g⁻¹ X g) = tr(X)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_append_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_append_letter","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**Markov cocycle on the Hecke image.**  Appending a generator\n`g = ρ(σ_i)` multiplies the Hecke image on the right:\n`ρ(β · σ_i) = ρ(β) · ρ(σ_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_nil","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L111-L114","doc":"The empty braid maps to the identity: `ρ(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage_append","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L102-L109","doc":"**Functoriality: the Hecke image is multiplicative under braid\nconcatenation.**  `ρ(β₁ β₂) = ρ(β₁) · ρ(β₂)`.  This is the genuine\nrepresentation-homomorphism property — the boundary holonomy is a\ngroup homomorphism from the braid monoid (under concatenation) to\n`G`, NOT a scalar power.  Proved from `braidWordHolonomy_append`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.braidWordHolonomy_eq_heckeImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.braidWordHolonomy_eq_heckeImage","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L97-L100","doc":"The boundary holonomy equals the braid's Hecke image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StokesSurfaceBoundary.heckeImage","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/nonabelian_stokes_surface_boundary_stokes.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**Boundary holonomy = Hecke image, by definition of the\nsurface→boundary reduction.**  The boundary holonomy of the braid\nword (the ordered product of its per-letter Hecke images) is the\nHecke image `ρ(β)` of the braid.  We *define* `heckeImage` to be the\nordered product and record the definitional equality with\n`braidWordHolonomy`; the content is that they are the SAME ordered\nproduct (no scalar `z^ℓ` collapse).\n\nThis is the provable surface→boundary piece: once Yekutieli's\ntheorem (the §3b-cond class below) reduces the surface-ordered\nexponential to the boundary ordered product, *that* product is\n`ρ(β)` by construction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}